# Media Player Development Patterns

## State Management
- Use [src/atoms/media-player.ts](mdc:src/atoms/media-player.ts) for all media player state
- Follow the established atom patterns for playback state
- Extend existing atoms rather than creating new ones
- Use the `updatePlaybackStateAtom` for state updates

## Component Structure
- Follow patterns in [src/components/media-player/](mdc:src/components/media-player/)
- Keep overlay components focused and composable
- Use the established hook patterns from [src/components/media-player/hooks/](mdc:src/components/media-player/hooks/)
- Export components through [src/components/media-player/index.ts](mdc:src/components/media-player/index.ts)

## Video Events
- Use HTML5 video events instead of useEffect for time updates
- Handle video state changes through event listeners
- Follow patterns in [src/components/media-player/media-player-video.tsx](mdc:src/components/media-player/media-player-video.tsx)

## Plex Integration
- Use existing PlexServerClient methods for media operations
- Follow timeline update patterns from [src/components/media-player/hooks/use-timeline-updates.ts](mdc:src/components/media-player/hooks/use-timeline-updates.ts)
- Handle play queue operations through established patterns

## Type Safety
- Use types from [src/types/media-player.ts](mdc:src/types/media-player.ts)
- Extend existing interfaces rather than creating new ones
- Ensure all media player operations are properly typed
